# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# NOT-2: `Notes` is on the party's own bar in both of the adventuring
# screen's modes, and nothing else on either screen is the seam's.
# The two bars are two strings in two places, the 3D view's and the area
# map's, and the splice is a separate pair of points for each (#221), so
# one of them working says nothing about the other. `A` is the game's own
# AREA command and swaps between them; both runs receive it, which is
# what lets this be a pair leg at all.

about Notes is on the 3D bar and on the area bar, and nowhere else
kind pair
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel

# No document, and no gate: since #290 the possession proof is the act,
# so what a leg says is a condition rather than a digest, and the run is
# made on the boot the challenge never stops (#291, #293).
code-wheel-answered
seam journal
until 232156800
every 25

# A screen may appear in the two runs a dump apart, because a repaint
# lands where it lands. One dump of slack, measured (#234).
slack 1

key L@7551
key A@7801
key A@9200

rect notes 273,192,311,199
rect bar 0,190,319,199

allow 0-7600 none

# The 3D view's bar: the difference is the six cells at its end.
allow 7625-9199 notes

# The swap redraws the whole screen and the two runs do it a few frames
# apart, so its own frames are named by nobody. The area map's words are a
# different length, so where the splice falls there is its own question and
# the assertion here is the row.
allow 9800-end bar
